---
import CalculatorLayout from "@/layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro"

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Is there one true ideal weight?",
    a: "No. Ideal body weight formulas give a rough reference range, not an exact target. Healthy weight depends on muscle mass, frame size, age, and overall health, so treat the result as a guideline.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which formulas does this use?",
    a: "It shows results from three well-known equations — Robinson (1983), Devine (1974), and Miller (1983) — which are all based on height and sex. The range between them gives a sensible reference band.",
  },
  {
    q: "Why does it only ask for height and sex?",
    a: "These classic formulas were designed to estimate a reference weight from height alone, with a small adjustment for sex. They do not account for body composition, which is why they are only a starting point.",
  },
  {
    q: "Should I aim for the exact number?",
    a: "Not necessarily. A healthy weight is a range, not a single figure. Use this alongside BMI and, ideally, guidance from a healthcare professional.",
  },
]
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Ideal Weight Calculator — Healthy Weight Range by Height"
  description="Estimate a healthy target weight range from your height and sex using the Robinson, Devine, and Miller formulas. Free ideal body weight calculator, metric & imperial."
  heading="Ideal Weight Calculator"
  intro="Estimate a healthy reference weight range based on your height and sex, using three established formulas."
  slug="ideal-weight"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <div slot="tool" class="tool">
    <div class="unit-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Measurement system">
      <button type="button" data-unit="metric" aria-pressed="true">Metric</button>
      <button type="button" data-unit="imperial" aria-pressed="false">Imperial</button>
    </div>

    <form novalidate data-calc>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="sex">Sex</label>
        <select id="sex" name="sex">
          <option value="male">Male</option>
          <option value="female">Female</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div data-metric>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="height-cm">Height (cm)</label>
          <input id="height-cm" name="heightCm" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="120" max="250" step="0.1" />
          <span class="error" data-error-for="height-cm" role="alert"></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div data-imperial hidden>
        <div class="field-row">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="height-ft">Height (ft)</label>
            <input id="height-ft" name="heightFt" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="4" max="8" step="1" />
            <span class="error" data-error-for="height-ft" role="alert"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="height-in">Height (in)</label>
            <input id="height-in" name="heightIn" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" max="11.9" step="0.1" />
            <span class="error" data-error-for="height-in" role="alert"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="actions">
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Calculate ideal weight</button>
        <button type="reset" class="btn btn-ghost">Reset</button>
      </div>
    </form>

    <div class="result" data-result hidden aria-live="polite">
      <p class="result-label">Estimated healthy weight range</p>
      <p class="result-value" data-value>—</p>
      <ul data-list></ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="formula">
    <p>Each formula starts from a base weight for a height of 5 feet (152.4 cm) and adds a fixed amount for every inch above that:</p>
    <p class="formula">Robinson: 52 kg (men) / 49 kg (women) + 1.9 / 1.7 kg per inch over 5 ft</p>
    <p class="formula">Devine: 50 kg (men) / 45.5 kg (women) + 2.3 kg per inch over 5 ft</p>
    <p class="formula">Miller: 56.2 kg (men) / 53.1 kg (women) + 1.41 / 1.36 kg per inch over 5 ft</p>
    <p>The calculator reports each result and uses the lowest and highest as a reference range.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="example">
    <p><strong>Person:</strong> a man 178 cm tall (about 70 inches, so 10 inches over 5 ft).</p>
    <p class="formula">Devine = 50 + 2.3 × 10 = 73.0 kg</p>
    <p class="formula">Robinson = 52 + 1.9 × 10 = 71.0 kg</p>
    <p>His reference range is roughly <strong>71–75 kg</strong> depending on the formula used.</p>
  </Fragment>
</CalculatorLayout>

<script>
  import { setupIdealWeight } from "@/scripts/ideal-weight"
  setupIdealWeight()
</script>
